<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Silingi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Silingi were a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> who probably lived in Silesia, which may take its name from them. They crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> in 406 and entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> in 409, receiving Baetica in 411, but were almost destroyed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a>, fighting for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, in 416–418. The survivors joined the Hasding Vandals.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/silingi.jpg" alt="Silingi" width="320" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexander G. Findlay · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Germania_-_New_York,_Harper_and_Brothers_1849.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
